<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Max von Oppenheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Max von Oppenheim was a German diplomat, orientalist and archaeologist. In 1899 he discovered the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-halaf">Tell Halaf</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, ancient Guzana, which he excavated from 1911 to 1913 and in 1929. He displayed the finds in his own museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, where they were shattered by bombing in 1943; the fragments were reassembled and exhibited again in 2011.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/max-von-oppenheim.jpg" alt="Max von Oppenheim" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oppenheim_Circa1917.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
